From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000011 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@libertyglobal.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 14:26:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] bus: bound synchronous RBUS set provider waits

The generic RBUS bus_set wrapper used rbus_set(), whose provider exchange has
no caller-selected timeout. During simultaneous tri-band EasyMesh onboarding
OneWifi applied a Vap_2.4G SOUTH subdoc, but the provider response was lost and
onewifi_em_agent remained blocked inside rbus_set for more than seven minutes.
That stopped the agent event queue, so the remaining radio subdocs and their
completion callbacks could never be processed.

Use the single-property form of rbus_setMultiExt with a five-second provider
timeout. It preserves the same value and immediate-commit semantics while
turning a lost provider response into a bounded error that the EasyMesh agent
can recover by replaying the WSC transaction.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 source/platform/rdkb/bus.c | 22 +++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/source/platform/rdkb/bus.c b/source/platform/rdkb/bus.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/source/platform/rdkb/bus.c
+++ b/source/platform/rdkb/bus.c
@@ -1275,7 +1275,10 @@ static bus_error_t bus_set(bus_handle_t *handle, char const *name, raw_data_t *
 {
     rbusError_t rc = RBUS_ERROR_SUCCESS;
+    rbusProperty_t property = NULL;
+    char *failed_parameter = NULL;
     VERIFY_NULL_WITH_RC(name);
 
+    const uint32_t provider_timeout_ms = 5000;
     rbusHandle_t p_rbus_handle = handle->u.rbus_handle;
 
     rbusValue_t value;
@@ -1307,11 +1310,22 @@ static bus_error_t bus_set(bus_handle_t *handle, char const *name, raw_data_t *
         break;
     };
 
-    rc = rbus_set(p_rbus_handle, name, value, NULL);
+    rbusProperty_Init(&property, name, value);
+    if (property == NULL) {
+        rbusValue_Release(value);
+        return bus_error_out_of_resources;
+    }
+
+    rc = rbus_setMultiExt(p_rbus_handle, 1, property, NULL,
+        provider_timeout_ms, &failed_parameter);
     if (rc != RBUS_ERROR_SUCCESS) {
-        wifi_util_dbg_print(WIFI_BUS, "%s:%d bus: rbus_set() failed:%d for name:%s\n",
-          __func__, __LINE__, rc, name);
+        wifi_util_error_print(WIFI_BUS,
+          "%s:%d bus: bounded rbus_set failed:%d for name:%s failed_parameter:%s\n",
+          __func__, __LINE__, rc, name,
+          failed_parameter != NULL ? failed_parameter : "none");
     }
+    free(failed_parameter);
+    rbusProperty_Release(property);
     rbusValue_Release(value);
     return convert_rbus_to_bus_error_code(rc);
 }
